[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3941455316","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-3941455316","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":3941455316,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7q7dXU","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T18:03:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T18:03:32Z","body":"To make the UI more familiar to VSCode users, would it be possible to have the replacement text input box be below the search input box? This would also make it easier to navigate to with the Tab key.\r\n\r\nSome other potential changes:\r\n- When the user types in the search box and presses enter, can the first search result grab focus?\r\n- Could it be changed so that just highlighting the search result (such as when going down the list) doesn't cause the script editor to grab focus? Currently you can't just arrow key through the search results","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3941455316/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3943278142","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-3943278142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":3943278142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rCaY-","user":{"login":"TheDying0fLight","id":95179191,"node_id":"U_kgDOBaxRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95179191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight","html_url":"https://github.com/TheDying0fLight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T08:15:45Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T08:15:45Z","body":"> To make the UI more familiar to VSCode users, would it be possible to have the replacement text input box be below the search input box? This would also make it easier to navigate to with the Tab key.\r\n\r\nI just got an idea for this and will try to implement it.\r\n\r\n> When the user types in the search box and presses enter, can the first search result grab focus?\r\n\r\nPersonally I prefer it to start a search, this seems more intuitive and is also how VSCode behaves. Maybe there could be a setting to choose this behavior.\r\n\r\n> Could it be changed so that just highlighting the search result (such as when going down the list) doesn't cause the script editor to grab focus? Currently you can't just arrow key through the search results\r\n\r\nI would also like this, but think its out of scope for this PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3943278142/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3945135157","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-3945135157","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":3945135157,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rJfw1","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T14:36:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T14:36:35Z","body":"> When the user types in the search box and presses enter, can the first search result grab focus?\r\n\r\n>> Personally I prefer it to start a search, this seems more intuitive and is also how VSCode behaves. Maybe there could be a setting to choose this behavior.\r\n\r\nI'd have to check again, but didn't your current implementation search after every key press in the search box? (I know I got into that state at some point at least)\r\n\r\n> Could it be changed so that just highlighting the search result (such as when going down the list) doesn't cause the script editor to grab focus? Currently you can't just arrow key through the search results\r\n\r\n>> I would also like this, but think its out of scope for this PR.\r\n\r\nAgreed","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3945135157/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946506308","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-3946506308","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":3946506308,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rOuhE","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T18:23:13Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T18:23:13Z","body":"I think the horizontal scroll should be disabled. The text may go out of bounds depending on current language.\r\n<img width=\"330\" height=\"260\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2d474d8a-e2b7-48e7-99a3-2366ac2b8959\" />\r\n\r\n> Personally I prefer it to start a search, this seems more intuitive and is also how VSCode behaves. Maybe there could be a setting to choose this behavior.\r\n\r\nVS Code indexes the whole project, or does some other magic so that searching is super fast (I'm honestly not sure how it can be that fast). Trying to do the same in Godot is a bad idea, as searching the whole project takes extremely long if there are many files.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946506308/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946638455","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-3946638455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":3946638455,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rPOx3","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T18:49:10Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T18:49:10Z","body":"I think instead of moving dialog to panel it will be good to have something like this https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/5544#issuecomment-1847419681. Similar functionality exists in PyCharm and it's really convenient.\r\nCombining dialog and panel will require rethink UI completely to make it usable.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946638455/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3949969025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-3949969025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":3949969025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rb76B","user":{"login":"TheDying0fLight","id":95179191,"node_id":"U_kgDOBaxRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95179191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight","html_url":"https://github.com/TheDying0fLight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T08:18:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T08:18:49Z","body":"> > Personally I prefer it to start a search, this seems more intuitive and is also how VSCode behaves. Maybe there could be a setting to choose this behavior.\r\n> \r\n> VS Code indexes the whole project, or does some other magic so that searching is super fast (I'm honestly not sure how it can be that fast). Trying to do the same in Godot is a bad idea, as searching the whole project takes extremely long if there are many files.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what you mean. If you mean searches can take a while and they should only be started when requested it should only be relevant for the automatic searches, since you have to at least be able to start searches manually. But since searches only iterate once each process step and don't block the main thread I think it is not problematic to start them whenever changes to the search parameters are made.\r\n\r\n> I think instead of moving dialog to panel it will be good to have something like this https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/5544#issuecomment-1847419681. Similar functionality exists in PyCharm and it's really convenient.\r\nCombining dialog and panel will require rethink UI completely to make it usable.\r\n\r\nIt seemed to me like progress to that implementation stalled and it would be more complicated. I think moving the dialog to the panel would already be an improvement (to the current popup solution) in the way it is implemented in the current version of the PR.\r\n\r\nBut I agree there are still some improvements to be made. What are the things in the UI you think need to be adjusted for this to be usable? Maybe I can address them. FYI I am currently trying to move the replace input under the search input in combination with loading the search parameters of a tab when it is opened so not only the replace text can be modified.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3949969025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3950081566","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-3950081566","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":3950081566,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rcXYe","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T08:41:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T08:41:37Z","body":"> What are the things in the UI you think need to be adjusted for this to be usable?\r\n\r\nIf I had known all details for proper implementation, I would have opened a PR for this😆 \r\nThe most obvious things are moving replace field under find (as you said), and replace \"Whole Worlds\"/ \"Match Case\" with icons (as other IDEs do), control visibility of Includes/Excludes using additional button (same as in VSCode), merge \"Include\" with \"Include the files with the extension\".\r\nAnd also Search Results (now it will be a wrong name for this dock) dock has sizing issues on small screens:\r\n<img width=\"972\" height=\"570\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/721317dc-c689-409d-af76-ecc202e66ac9\" />\r\n\r\n> as searching the whole project takes extremely long if there are many files.\r\n\r\nThat is why in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/5544#issuecomment-1847419681 there is a controllable limit for search.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3950081566/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974423979","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-3974423979","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":3974423979,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7s5OWr","user":{"login":"TheDying0fLight","id":95179191,"node_id":"U_kgDOBaxRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95179191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight","html_url":"https://github.com/TheDying0fLight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T18:31:15Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T18:47:47Z","body":"> merge \"Include\" with \"Include the files with the extension\".\r\n\r\nDo you have an example how this could look?\r\n\r\n> And also Search Results (...) dock has sizing issues on small screens:\r\n\r\nI can see \"fun\" in the right panel being cut of (should be better now) and that less of the results is shown (could reduce min size of left panel but not by a lot). Is there something else I am missing?\r\n\r\nOther than that the suggestions should be implemented now. I also added a \"Result Limit\" option which defaults to 1000, if a search is limited by this it stays active and continues when the limit is increased. Some icons are from https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-icons (they haven't been updated in a while) which we are allowed to use as far as I can tell, open for better suggestions.\r\n\r\n<img height=\"200\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/55f1c5a8-00c2-4077-80ea-93124ca1eddf\" />\r\n<img height=\"100\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/20dfb9ea-994f-4443-b678-22887967970b\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3974423979/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4896690119","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-4896690119","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":4896690119,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI92Pxw","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T19:10:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T19:18:14Z","body":"The empty panel with vertical 3dots button looks weird.\r\n<img width=\"467\" height=\"355\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2cc664c5-760c-4675-a475-9e02f841a887\" />\r\nThe space is unused anyway, so couldn't this be always visible? Or you could use FoldableContainer maybe, idk.\r\n\r\n> Also I removed the Replace in Files shortcut since the mode can now be toggled quickly and it was inconsistent in being available in the script editor but not the global shortcuts. It would be possible to add a new shortcut for toggling the replace mode when the Search Results panel is open.\r\n\r\nThe option is not very discoverable in the current state. I think a menu option/shortcut + global action should still exist.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4896690119/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4906902512","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-4906902512","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":4906902512,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJHlj8A","user":{"login":"TheDying0fLight","id":95179191,"node_id":"U_kgDOBaxRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95179191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight","html_url":"https://github.com/TheDying0fLight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-07T17:53:13Z","updated_at":"2026-07-09T21:07:28Z","body":"> The empty panel with vertical 3dots button looks weird.\r\n> The space is unused anyway, so couldn't this be always visible? Or you could use FoldableContainer maybe, idk.\r\n\r\nI think not always showing the less often used options helps reduce the \"visual load\" on the user.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"300\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/973db23b-6c7c-4f04-8ecb-38350d2be1d9\" /> <img width=\"300\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81ba0bfa-fa47-4061-bb6f-1a10a1a3391c\" />\r\n\r\nThis is how a FoldableContainer would look. The background color does not fit yet (don't know what would be the best way to give it a flat theme), otherwise it looks good to me. What do you think?\r\n\r\n> > Also I removed the Replace in Files shortcut since the mode can now be toggled quickly and it was inconsistent in being available in the script editor but not the global shortcuts. It would be possible to add a new shortcut for toggling the replace mode when the Search Results panel is open.\r\n> \r\n> The option is not very discoverable in the current state.\r\n\r\nI disagree with it not being discoverable since the button to toggle it is directly besides the search field.\r\n\r\n> I think a menu option/shortcut + global action should still exist.\r\n\r\nOk I will re-add it and make it consistent with the search shortcut","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4906902512/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4934028053","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-4934028053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":4934028053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJhdLFQ","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-10T09:39:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-10T09:39:51Z","body":"Changing search tabs clears the folder field (it does correctly preserve other filters).\r\n\r\n> What do you think?\r\n\r\nLooks fine IMO. You could consider using SCROLL_MODE_RESERVE in the scroll container, because the content jumps when unfolding.\r\n\r\n> I disagree with it not being discoverable since the button to toggle it is directly besides the search field.\r\n\r\nIt's very easy to miss though. But well, not for me to decide.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4934028053/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011374591","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-5011374591","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":5011374591,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKrOB_w","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T13:09:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T13:09:37Z","body":"> The 'replace' and 'remove result' buttons on the right of the results lack hover states:\r\n\r\nThat's unrelated to this PR, it was like that before.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011374591/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011892900","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-5011892900","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":5011892900,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKrtqpA","user":{"login":"TheDying0fLight","id":95179191,"node_id":"U_kgDOBaxRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95179191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight","html_url":"https://github.com/TheDying0fLight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T15:52:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T15:52:33Z","body":"> The 'show replace' button in front of the search is pretty bad usability. At the surface, nothing hints at that button enabling the 'replace' mode of the find in files panel. Here's a mockup / suggestion for what I think is a better design and which I don't think takes a lot of rework on the UI:\r\n\r\n@KoBeWi also mentioned this so this should be changed. Though I feel like having the `Search`/`Replace` `LineEdit`s directly above each other helps with visual clarity (I don't have a good idea for this with a different toggle option), but maybe that's because I am biased since I mainly use VSCode which does it like this. I will use your suggestion for now\r\n\r\n> I see no reason for the 'Filters' section to be foldable, and folded in by default. The big empty space upon first opening the panel feels pretty useless. Might as well remove the foldable state, keep the filters as a header, and have it unfolded at all times. (already in the above mockup)\r\n\r\nThe idea was to reduce \"visual load\" by hiding less often used features. But since @KoBeWi also suggested removing it I will do that\r\n\r\n> The checkboxes for what files to search are unfortunately positioned under the 'Excludes' property which feels like a header, creating a bit of a false sense that the checkboxes are for files to ignore. best move those checkboxes under the 'Includes' property instead. (already in the mockup above)\r\n\r\nWould switching the `Includes` and `Excludes` text boxes be fine? Then the extensions can grow into the empty space and don't move UI elements when new ones are added\r\n\r\n> Once there's tabs, I'd expect the 'create new tab' button (the button with the plus icon) to move to the right of the tabs:\r\n\r\nI wanted to do this but at the time couldn't find a good way to add it to the tabs. I will look at it again\r\n\r\n> … and now that I'm thinking about it, why not just always have tabs, even when there's a single one, and add the create button next to the right-most tab? Then there doesn't have to be any fiddling with the create tab button at all.\r\n\r\nI didn't do this because I think for people who don't use multiple searches having the additional space from the hidden tabs is helpful","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011892900/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5012451793","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-5012451793","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":5012451793,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKsPx0Q","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T18:37:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T18:37:15Z","body":"> Would switching the Includes and Excludes text boxes be fine?\r\n\r\nYeah!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5012451793/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5024799885","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116560#issuecomment-5024799885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116560","id":5024799885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABK4BcjQ","user":{"login":"TheDying0fLight","id":95179191,"node_id":"U_kgDOBaxRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95179191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight","html_url":"https://github.com/TheDying0fLight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheDying0fLi